WEBVTT


00:00:33.048 --> 00:00:34.488
The question of happiness


00:00:34.649 --> 00:00:36.613
has preoccupied
philosophers, poets


00:00:36.768 --> 00:00:39.332
and pharmaceutical companies
for thousands of years.


00:00:40.488 --> 00:00:43.008
Clearly, it's a tricky one.


00:00:43.167 --> 00:00:45.928
When I graduated from
design school three years ago,


00:00:46.087 --> 00:00:48.815
I had a definite plan.


00:00:48.967 --> 00:00:52.568
Couple months at home,
put together a kickass portfolio,


00:00:52.727 --> 00:00:55.771
then I'd take Manhattan
by storm.


00:00:58.126 --> 00:00:59.687
And here is home.


00:01:00.687 --> 00:01:02.127
West Orange, New Jersey.


00:01:02.286 --> 00:01:03.891
Nice, huh?


00:01:05.487 --> 00:01:08.607
OK, it's not Manhattan,
but, like I say, it's temporary.


00:01:08.766 --> 00:01:12.530
I grew up here
with two families.


00:01:12.686 --> 00:01:15.370
That's my dad in blue,
and that's his best friend, Terry.


00:01:15.526 --> 00:01:17.370
The Inseparables.


00:01:17.526 --> 00:01:20.614
They go jogging together
three times a week without fail.


00:01:20.765 --> 00:01:22.926
You can set your clock by it.


00:01:23.085 --> 00:01:25.846
You could say life in the Oranges
is dependable.


00:01:26.005 --> 00:01:27.969
I can't believe
you made me do this.


00:01:28.125 --> 00:01:30.853
Good for your appetite.
See you in an hour.


00:01:31.005 --> 00:01:34.093
You can depend on Terry
to have a gadget for everything.


00:01:34.245 --> 00:01:36.972
Walked 1.2 miles.
Only stopped twice.


00:01:37.124 --> 00:01:38.445
That's great, honey.


00:01:38.604 --> 00:01:40.491
And you can
depend on Cathy


00:01:40.644 --> 00:01:42.444
to never hear
a single word he says.


00:01:42.604 --> 00:01:44.284
Make sure you put your bicycle
in the garage.


00:01:44.444 --> 00:01:46.288
And pull the pork
out of the freezer, honey.


00:01:47.483 --> 00:01:51.651
Across the street,
our house.


00:01:51.804 --> 00:01:54.171
Every year,
my mom gets more involved


00:01:54.324 --> 00:01:55.687
with her carolling group.


00:01:55.844 --> 00:01:57.644
They start rehearsing
in August.


00:01:57.803 --> 00:01:59.363
# Jingle bells
Jingle all the way... #


00:01:59.523 --> 00:02:02.088
And every year, my dad
hates them a little bit more.


00:02:05.123 --> 00:02:08.964
OK, sure. I'm still here.
I'm a few years behind in my plan.


00:02:09.123 --> 00:02:10.890
But you can't
rush these things.


00:02:11.043 --> 00:02:13.891
Portfolios need
to be perfect, right?


00:02:14.042 --> 00:02:16.682
Plus I have a day job
working in furniture, so...


00:02:16.842 --> 00:02:20.202
...as far as I was concerned,
everything was on track.


00:02:20.362 --> 00:02:23.406
# Happy birthday to you... #


00:02:23.561 --> 00:02:26.409
That is, until what
happened... happened


00:02:26.562 --> 00:02:28.646
Nina Ostroff.


00:02:28.801 --> 00:02:31.485
When all this started,
she was at a safe distance,


00:02:31.641 --> 00:02:33.681
3, 000 miles away
in San Francisco.


00:02:33.841 --> 00:02:37.485
I Happy birthday to you. I


00:02:37.641 --> 00:02:39.965
Make a wish, babe.


00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:49.608
And I was the fifth wheel


00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:52.008
to our parents'
regular Saturday foursome.


00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:53.840
Say it again.


00:02:53.999 --> 00:02:55.287
OK.


00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:57.763
Un coup de birch.


00:02:57.920 --> 00:02:59.403
Hey, Vanny.


00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:01.043
I read the most
interesting article


00:03:01.199 --> 00:03:02.967
called 'The IKEA Conspiracy',


00:03:03.119 --> 00:03:04.724
which you'd be
really fascinated by.


00:03:04.879 --> 00:03:06.200
- What it imagines is a...
- Terry?


00:03:06.359 --> 00:03:07.842
We need to call Nina.
We said 9:30.


00:03:07.999 --> 00:03:09.439
I'm on it.


00:03:09.599 --> 00:03:11.803
Vanessa, did you look at
that one-bedroom in Fort Lee?


00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:15.123
Yeah. It was, um, like a closet
in the basement.


00:03:15.278 --> 00:03:16.642
There's always something, honey.


00:03:16.798 --> 00:03:18.119
Don't be so choosy.
Nothing's perfect.


00:03:18.278 --> 00:03:20.439
There was, you know,
one window.


00:03:20.598 --> 00:03:22.442
- Paige, did I tell you...
- No room to breathe.


00:03:22.598 --> 00:03:24.278
...that Joan Marshack
was the listing agent on that?


00:03:24.438 --> 00:03:27.242
David, you are going
to really love this.


00:03:27.398 --> 00:03:32.199
This speaker box communicates
wirelessly with my cell phone.


00:03:32.358 --> 00:03:34.442
And guess where
I read about it first.


00:03:34.597 --> 00:03:36.605
'Consumer Reports'. Thank you
so much for the subscription.


00:03:36.758 --> 00:03:39.006
- I'm really enjoying it.
- You are consumingly welcome.


00:03:39.157 --> 00:03:42.245
I don't even have to take
my cell phone out of my pocket.


00:03:42.397 --> 00:03:43.718
Watch.


00:03:43.877 --> 00:03:45.721
Dial Nina.


00:03:45.877 --> 00:03:47.317
Please repeat request.


00:03:47.476 --> 00:03:48.797
Dial Nina.


00:03:48.957 --> 00:03:51.041
Maybe your pants
are blocking the signal.


00:03:51.196 --> 00:03:52.636
They're cotton.


00:03:54.076 --> 00:03:56.716
Nina's cell phone, dialling.


00:03:58.516 --> 00:04:01.517
Nina - their daughter
and my best friend


00:04:01.676 --> 00:04:03.684
from ages 0
to high school.


00:04:03.836 --> 00:04:06.236
We spent hours together
planning our big escape.


00:04:06.396 --> 00:04:08.360
I'm gonna live in New York.


00:04:08.515 --> 00:04:09.836
And Paris.


00:04:09.995 --> 00:04:12.243
And I'm gonna be a famous chef
and have a million lovers


00:04:12.395 --> 00:04:13.716
who'll take me
all over the world


00:04:13.875 --> 00:04:16.003
so I never have to come back
to New Jersey again.


00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:18.882
It's like
there's no air here, right?


00:04:19.034 --> 00:04:20.639
Totally.


00:04:23.314 --> 00:04:24.755
You'll come too, right?


00:04:24.914 --> 00:04:26.834
Are you kidding?


00:04:28.035 --> 00:04:29.802
Until sophomore year,


00:04:29.954 --> 00:04:34.242
when she abandoned me for
Liz Gaines and the Fun Bunch.


00:04:36.834 --> 00:04:41.034
She also kissed and later gave
a hand job to Peter Fortunate.


00:04:41.194 --> 00:04:44.314
I'd been secretly
in love with him forever.


00:04:45.433 --> 00:04:47.397
Then, just as her parents
were lining her up


00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:49.353
at some lame college
in Pennsylvania,


00:04:49.513 --> 00:04:51.957
she decided she was
going to travel the world.


00:04:52.113 --> 00:04:54.557
Or at least those parts


00:04:54.712 --> 00:04:56.632
that were out of
her mothefs cell phone range.


00:05:00.032 --> 00:05:01.679
Hello?


00:05:01.832 --> 00:05:04.232
Happy birthday, sweetie!


00:05:04.392 --> 00:05:06.040
- Happy birthday!
- Happy birthday, Nina.


00:05:06.192 --> 00:05:09.040
It's David and Paige.
Vanessa's here too.


00:05:09.192 --> 00:05:10.916
It's true. I'm here.


00:05:11.072 --> 00:05:12.360
Hey, Ethan.


00:05:12.511 --> 00:05:15.239
I think Nina's fucking parents
are on the phone.


00:05:16.992 --> 00:05:19.436
I didn't know I was having
a party. It was a surprise.


00:05:19.591 --> 00:05:21.675
Honey, we can't hear you.


00:05:21.831 --> 00:05:24.438
Ethan threw me
a surprise party.


00:05:24.591 --> 00:05:26.315
It's so great.


00:05:26.471 --> 00:05:27.792
Did you guys get
the pictures I sent?


00:05:27.951 --> 00:05:29.675
Yes, we did.


00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:31.511
More young men should have earrings
in their face.


00:05:31.671 --> 00:05:34.071
What? I'm sorry, I can't
hear you. Am I on speaker?


00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:37.951
Nina, what day are you
flying in for Thanksgiving?


00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:41.154
Thanksgiving. Mom, um...


00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:45.154
Uh, I don't think I'm gonna
make it for Thanksgiving.


00:05:45.309 --> 00:05:48.430
Ethan's photography show's
next weekend, and it's a big deal.


00:05:48.589 --> 00:05:50.389
Sweetie, we haven't
seen you for two years.


00:05:50.549 --> 00:05:51.913
You haven't been home
in five years.


00:05:52.069 --> 00:05:53.794
Since we visited you.
That's a long time.


00:05:53.949 --> 00:05:55.269
Um...


00:05:55.429 --> 00:05:57.437
Can you take me
off speaker, please?


00:05:57.589 --> 00:05:59.030
Sorry, sweetie,
I'd have to disconnect you


00:05:59.189 --> 00:06:01.153
to take you off speaker -
it's a very complex system.


00:06:01.309 --> 00:06:02.313
OK.


00:06:03.708 --> 00:06:06.557
Look, you're not
gonna like this, but...


00:06:06.708 --> 00:06:08.792
Ethan and I
are getting married.


00:06:08.948 --> 00:06:12.069
He proposed two weeks ago
on his birthday.


00:06:12.228 --> 00:06:13.832
He took me out
to Baker Beach,


00:06:13.988 --> 00:06:15.308
which overlooks
the Golden Gate Bridge,


00:06:15.468 --> 00:06:17.312
and he got down on one knee
and everything.


00:06:17.468 --> 00:06:20.872
- He proposed on his birthday?
- I don't understand.


00:06:21.028 --> 00:06:22.795
I'm in love with him.


00:06:23.788 --> 00:06:25.796
That's really great,
sweetie, but...


00:06:25.947 --> 00:06:27.988
You're only 24 years old.


00:06:28.147 --> 00:06:29.991
Nobody gets married
at 24 anymore.


00:06:30.147 --> 00:06:31.991
People get married
when they're 17.


00:06:32.147 --> 00:06:33.511
Not white girls
from New Jersey.


00:06:33.667 --> 00:06:35.227
- Shh!
- Would you listen to yourself?


00:06:35.387 --> 00:06:36.991
No, you listen -
you have made some


00:06:37.146 --> 00:06:39.350
very questionable decisions
in your life.


00:06:39.506 --> 00:06:40.870
Please don't
add to the list


00:06:41.026 --> 00:06:44.715
by marrying some loser kid
with zero future.


00:06:44.866 --> 00:06:47.834
OK. I have an idea.


00:06:47.986 --> 00:06:52.034
If you think he's such a loser,
then don't come to the wedding!


00:06:56.465 --> 00:06:58.145
Jesus, turn that thing down!


00:07:00.505 --> 00:07:04.946
Down volume!
Down volume!


00:07:05.105 --> 00:07:08.345
- Oh, God!
- Down volume!


00:07:14.265 --> 00:07:17.505
You guys, it's getting late.
The party's over, OK?


00:07:17.664 --> 00:07:19.432
Love you. 'Bye.


00:07:19.584 --> 00:07:21.068
Amy, did you see Ethan?


00:07:22.224 --> 00:07:23.665
Baby?


00:07:23.824 --> 00:07:25.984
Ethan?


00:07:29.943 --> 00:07:31.351
Ethan?


00:07:31.503 --> 00:07:33.827
Uh, it's...
Gimme a sec.


00:07:33.983 --> 00:07:36.351
Come on. I want to
get everybody out of here.


00:07:50.622 --> 00:07:52.662
Hey, how's it going with
the, uh, couples counsellor?


00:07:52.822 --> 00:07:55.386
I don't know.
She's so non-specific.


00:07:55.542 --> 00:07:58.182
It's like talking to fog.


00:07:58.342 --> 00:08:00.502
David and I know
where we stand with each other.


00:08:00.661 --> 00:08:03.029
That's how we've lasted this long.
Somehow, it works.


00:08:03.182 --> 00:08:06.706
Well, don't look at me.
I just pretend Terry's invisible.


00:08:06.861 --> 00:08:09.381
- Notice anything different?
- I sure do.


00:08:09.541 --> 00:08:11.265
Nice new mini fridge.


00:08:11.421 --> 00:08:12.862
I think it really
ties the room together.


00:08:13.021 --> 00:08:15.465
-It's the Max 5950.
-It's the one you recommended.


00:08:15.621 --> 00:08:17.508
From the patio series.
Good move.


00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:19.701
Let's take a look
in the mini ice compartment.


00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:22.900
Oh, boy.
It's really big, isn't it?


00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:26.148
Now, this stuff is huge
in Europe.


00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:28.787
And we've just landed
the American campaign.


00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:30.500
- No kidding? Congrats.
- Thanks.


00:08:30.659 --> 00:08:32.667
Russians like it
for breakfast.


00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:37.067
Before the devil
knows you're dead.


00:08:40.419 --> 00:08:42.186
Boy, it's, um...


00:08:42.339 --> 00:08:43.866
Well...
Really not very good, is it?


00:08:44.019 --> 00:08:45.863
-It's not good at all. No.
- No.


00:08:51.459 --> 00:08:52.942
What's up
with these sheets?


00:08:54.258 --> 00:08:56.299
You, um...


00:08:56.458 --> 00:08:58.258
...spending a little extra time
out here?


00:08:58.418 --> 00:09:00.579
Just a couple of nights a week.


00:09:00.738 --> 00:09:03.106
Late-night TV.


00:09:27.017 --> 00:09:29.821
You've gotta be
fucking kidding me.


00:09:36.816 --> 00:09:38.856
Oh, sh...


00:09:51.175 --> 00:09:52.702
Nina? Wow!


00:09:52.855 --> 00:09:55.659
- David. Hi.
- It's been so long.


00:09:57.094 --> 00:09:59.855
I thought you weren't
coming back for Thanksgiving.


00:10:00.015 --> 00:10:01.902
Yeah, well...


00:10:02.054 --> 00:10:03.822
Um...


00:10:05.374 --> 00:10:08.539
Are my parents here?
Locked out.


00:10:08.694 --> 00:10:10.942
They're in the back.


00:10:11.094 --> 00:10:13.734
Last day of barbecue season.


00:10:16.173 --> 00:10:18.454
What's going on?


00:10:18.613 --> 00:10:20.217
- You OK?
- David?


00:10:20.373 --> 00:10:22.773
Paige wants to know what
you did with the tong thing.


00:10:24.173 --> 00:10:25.853
Hi, Mom.


00:10:26.013 --> 00:10:29.133
I'm back for Thanksgiving.


00:10:29.292 --> 00:10:31.453
We turned it into
a second den.


00:10:31.612 --> 00:10:33.260
If your father's
in the first den


00:10:33.412 --> 00:10:34.972
and I want some privacy,
I come here.


00:10:35.133 --> 00:10:36.496
Honey,
I have this really cool


00:10:36.653 --> 00:10:37.973
self-inflating mattress.


00:10:38.132 --> 00:10:40.697
It fits perfectly in the corner
and it is really comfy.


00:10:43.092 --> 00:10:45.580
But, you know, we have your
old bed frame out there in the...


00:10:45.732 --> 00:10:47.619
...in the garage -
I can set it up for you.


00:10:47.772 --> 00:10:49.900
- Take me two...two se...
- No, that's fine.


00:10:50.051 --> 00:10:51.971
I'll only be here
a few days.


00:10:52.131 --> 00:10:54.576
Why? Where are you
going to now?


00:10:54.731 --> 00:10:57.176
I don't know.


00:10:58.931 --> 00:11:00.851
I haven't figured it out yet.


00:11:01.011 --> 00:11:02.898
Well, why don't you
stay here for a while?


00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:04.491
I don't care -
it's not like we haven't


00:11:04.651 --> 00:11:06.812
gotten used
to you being gone.


00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:09.410
Can you hold off
on the guilt trips


00:11:09.571 --> 00:11:10.891
for just a little while,
please?


00:11:11.050 --> 00:11:12.611
I've had
a rough couple days.


00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:17.130
I'd never seen Nina
with her tail between her legs.


00:11:17.289 --> 00:11:19.930
But I didn't
have time to gloat.


00:11:20.090 --> 00:11:23.134
Back on our side of the street,
we had our own problems.


00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:24.654
That's not what I'm saying.


00:11:24.810 --> 00:11:26.774
- What about Christmas?
- Come on, Paige.


00:11:26.929 --> 00:11:30.050
- I'm trying here.
- Oh. Now I'm not trying.


00:11:31.289 --> 00:11:32.936
Can't we have
a simple conversation?


00:11:33.089 --> 00:11:36.973
- I make one suggestion...
- I don't want to go down there.


00:11:37.129 --> 00:11:39.890
- You seem oblivious...
- Come on, Paige...


00:11:46.888 --> 00:11:49.136
I apologise
for what I said about Ethan.


00:11:49.288 --> 00:11:52.049
- Were you waiting for me?
- I'm not your enemy. Nina!


00:11:52.208 --> 00:11:53.692
When you're a parent
some day,


00:11:53.848 --> 00:11:55.256
you'll understand
what it feels like


00:11:55.407 --> 00:11:57.207
to have your child hate you.


00:11:58.248 --> 00:12:00.135
In case you're wondering,
that's your cue to say,


00:12:00.287 --> 00:12:01.608
"I don't hate you, Mom."


00:12:01.767 --> 00:12:03.175
I don't hate you.


00:12:03.327 --> 00:12:08.052
I just get furious
thinking someone has hurt you.


00:12:11.687 --> 00:12:15.091
Don't think I'm crazy.
This is just a thought. But, uh...


00:12:16.487 --> 00:12:18.854
Toby's coming home
for Thanksgiving.


00:12:20.606 --> 00:12:23.127
- Oh, my God.
- He's gotten very attractive.


00:12:23.286 --> 00:12:24.649
That's all I'm saying.


00:12:24.806 --> 00:12:26.726
He works for
the Federal Trade Commission.


00:12:26.886 --> 00:12:28.249
Terrific. You date him.


00:12:28.406 --> 00:12:30.206
Well, it's not like you two
don't have history.


00:12:30.366 --> 00:12:31.894
- We kissed!
- Yeah.


00:12:32.045 --> 00:12:33.366
Once, like, 10 years ago.


00:12:33.525 --> 00:12:35.969
Can you at least let me unpack
before pimping me out?


00:12:36.126 --> 00:12:38.810
OK, fine. But I'm gonna
tell you this for your own good.


00:12:38.965 --> 00:12:41.769
You need to have a real
relationship with a real man.


00:12:41.925 --> 00:12:44.369
It's time you grew up already!
Stop running away.


00:12:44.524 --> 00:12:47.525
You know, you're right.
I'm being selfish.


00:12:47.684 --> 00:12:49.125
The best thing
I can do right now


00:12:49.285 --> 00:12:50.605
is fulfil
your insane suburban fantasy


00:12:50.764 --> 00:12:52.085
where I marry
your best friend's son.


00:12:52.244 --> 00:12:55.649
Now, you go call the catering hall
and I'll lube my vagina.


00:12:55.804 --> 00:12:58.248
That was uncalled for.


00:12:58.404 --> 00:12:59.887
Uh, there's 12 of us
in the delegation.


00:13:00.044 --> 00:13:01.604
I'm really just...
just assisting my boss.


00:13:01.764 --> 00:13:03.728
But the goal is to
tie our trade agreements


00:13:03.883 --> 00:13:05.651
to stricter
environmental regulations


00:13:05.803 --> 00:13:07.931
since things
are kind of a mess over there.


00:13:09.323 --> 00:13:11.887
- China. That's great.
- Yeah, thanks.


00:13:12.043 --> 00:13:13.843
You are gonna have
a great experience.


00:13:14.003 --> 00:13:16.326
- Yeah. Yeah.
- It's, like, a 30-hour flight.


00:13:16.483 --> 00:13:18.523
- Honey, what about Christmas?
- Don't worry, Mom.


00:13:18.682 --> 00:13:20.003
I fly back on the 24th.


00:13:20.162 --> 00:13:21.690
That sounds
really great, Toby.


00:13:21.842 --> 00:13:24.603
I hear that ultimate frisbee
is exploding over there.


00:13:24.762 --> 00:13:26.846
In China. The, uh...


00:13:27.003 --> 00:13:30.484
The Beijing club team
came in second at the World's.


00:13:30.642 --> 00:13:32.246
If I see a game,
I'll let 'em know


00:13:32.402 --> 00:13:35.445
I grew up across the street
from the guy who invented it.


00:13:35.602 --> 00:13:39.170
Well. It wasn't just me. It was
also Jared Kass and, uh...


00:13:39.322 --> 00:13:40.969
- Honey?
- Joel Silver.


00:13:41.122 --> 00:13:42.726
Of course, Joel gets
most of the, you know...


00:13:42.881 --> 00:13:45.566
...most of the play, being
a big movie producer and all.


00:13:45.721 --> 00:13:47.969
Finally!


00:13:50.401 --> 00:13:52.529
Where there's dessert,
there's hope.


00:13:56.680 --> 00:13:59.921
Your mom told me about what
happened with that Ethan guy.


00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:02.000
You OK?


00:14:05.480 --> 00:14:06.800
Yeah.


00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:09.088
I'm good, thanks.


00:14:10.399 --> 00:14:12.319
So, what about you?


00:14:12.479 --> 00:14:14.488
How's the liquor
advertising business going?


00:14:14.639 --> 00:14:16.407
Still pushing booze
onto minors?


00:14:16.559 --> 00:14:19.003
Yes, I am.


00:14:19.159 --> 00:14:20.479
Actually,
I just got a promotion.


00:14:20.639 --> 00:14:22.166
I'm now executive
vice-president,


00:14:22.319 --> 00:14:23.639
creative accounts.


00:14:23.798 --> 00:14:25.326
Congratulations.


00:14:25.479 --> 00:14:27.607
Was that something
you wanted?


00:14:27.758 --> 00:14:29.799
Not really.


00:14:29.958 --> 00:14:31.878
You want me to spoon this
onto the plates?


00:14:32.038 --> 00:14:33.522
Please.


00:14:33.678 --> 00:14:37.159
Uh... Don't just eat it
right out the carton.


00:14:39.878 --> 00:14:42.758
Is it good?


00:14:44.957 --> 00:14:46.365
- It's cold.
- What?


00:14:46.518 --> 00:14:50.522
Hey. I brought that ice-cream
for the pies.


00:14:50.677 --> 00:14:52.564
He made me eat it.


00:14:53.797 --> 00:14:55.565
Well, Cathy wants
to serve dessert.


00:14:55.717 --> 00:14:57.485
Will you please
bring in some plates?


00:14:59.756 --> 00:15:02.124
I still need Christmas lists
from everyone by tonight.


00:15:02.277 --> 00:15:03.597
I'm leaving early tomorrow.


00:15:03.756 --> 00:15:05.764
- Black Friday.
- Don't make fun.


00:15:05.916 --> 00:15:09.724
Last year, I got there at 3am
and I was still 210 in line.


00:15:09.876 --> 00:15:11.316
Why would anyone
want to shop


00:15:11.476 --> 00:15:13.081
on the same day
as everyone else?


00:15:13.236 --> 00:15:15.156
I hear that
they have fist fights


00:15:15.316 --> 00:15:17.040
and people throw their children
at each other.


00:15:17.196 --> 00:15:20.044
Terry! No.
It's really a very...


00:15:20.195 --> 00:15:24.079
Very communal, Christmassy
experience. It's beautiful.


00:15:24.235 --> 00:15:25.599
Listen, I know it's late,


00:15:25.755 --> 00:15:27.239
but I think
we should have a toast.


00:15:27.395 --> 00:15:29.763
It's Thanksgiving. We have
so much to be thankful for.


00:15:29.915 --> 00:15:32.075
Toby is going to China.


00:15:32.234 --> 00:15:33.555
Very exciting.


00:15:33.715 --> 00:15:36.279
Nina is finally
back at home.


00:15:36.435 --> 00:15:39.196
And Vanessa
continues to live among us,


00:15:39.354 --> 00:15:41.034
bringing us joy every day.


00:15:41.194 --> 00:15:43.081
To the Walling
and Ostroff clans.


00:15:43.234 --> 00:15:46.802
Who knew that two families
could get this close?


00:15:46.954 --> 00:15:48.274
Hear, hear.


00:15:48.433 --> 00:15:50.998
I still think we could be
a little closer.


00:15:52.993 --> 00:15:55.274
Well said.


00:15:57.313 --> 00:16:00.401
Man, I thought your mom
was going to applaud


00:16:00.553 --> 00:16:01.874
when she saw us
leave together.


00:16:02.033 --> 00:16:04.881
The woman
is a total lunatic.


00:16:05.033 --> 00:16:06.877
In the first three years
I was gone,


00:16:07.033 --> 00:16:08.833
she sent me
letters from the cat.


00:16:08.992 --> 00:16:11.240
"Dear Nina,
Don't be difficult.


00:16:11.393 --> 00:16:12.800
"Call your mother
on her birthday."


00:16:12.952 --> 00:16:15.320
That's great, actually.
I kind of like that.


00:16:15.472 --> 00:16:17.960
Now you understand
why I never came back.


00:16:18.992 --> 00:16:21.075
Yeah. No, I hear ya. But...


00:16:21.232 --> 00:16:23.752
I'm glad you did.


00:16:25.071 --> 00:16:26.119
Shut up.


00:16:30.271 --> 00:16:31.995
Dance with me.


00:16:33.631 --> 00:16:35.115
Totally.


00:16:38.791 --> 00:16:40.351
You OK?


00:16:40.510 --> 00:16:41.831
I need to get some water.


00:16:41.991 --> 00:16:43.878
- Can I get some water?
- OK. Sit down, wild man.


00:16:44.031 --> 00:16:47.512
I'm sorry.
I'm so sorry.


00:16:52.630 --> 00:16:54.354
- Hey.
- Toby needs water.


00:16:54.509 --> 00:16:56.277
What are you doing up?


00:16:56.429 --> 00:16:59.637
Just watching a little TV
in the man cave.


00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:02.910
- Man cave?
- It's the pool house.


00:17:03.069 --> 00:17:05.830
I got one of those
worldwide sports...


00:17:05.989 --> 00:17:08.117
...something something package
your dad recommended.


00:17:08.269 --> 00:17:10.473
There's this
Korean basketball league


00:17:10.629 --> 00:17:12.276
which is completely crazy.


00:17:12.429 --> 00:17:14.557
You know, it's not good
to eat peanut butter


00:17:14.708 --> 00:17:16.029
this late at night.


00:17:16.188 --> 00:17:17.509
It'll make you fat.


00:17:17.668 --> 00:17:19.512
I'm not fat.


00:17:19.668 --> 00:17:21.393
You will be if you
keep eating like that


00:17:21.548 --> 00:17:22.868
at 2:00 in the morning.


00:17:23.028 --> 00:17:24.675
And where'd you pick
this little factoid up?


00:17:24.828 --> 00:17:26.432
I worked in
a lot of restaurants.


00:17:26.587 --> 00:17:28.715
Restaurants
that serve peanut butter?


00:17:28.868 --> 00:17:30.876
Look, do whatever you want.


00:17:31.028 --> 00:17:33.472
I'm just saying
that you wouldn't look good fat.


00:17:35.947 --> 00:17:37.834
I should get back downstairs.


00:17:37.987 --> 00:17:39.754
Yeah, make your mother
very happy. You know that.


00:17:39.907 --> 00:17:41.227
It's what I live for.


00:18:28.624 --> 00:18:30.544
- Hi.
- Hi.


00:18:31.744 --> 00:18:33.271
What happened to Toby?


00:18:33.424 --> 00:18:35.344
I cut him up
in little pieces


00:18:35.504 --> 00:18:37.304
and put him in the fridge
for later.


00:18:44.503 --> 00:18:46.063
Who's playing?


00:18:47.663 --> 00:18:49.507
I have no idea.


00:18:49.663 --> 00:18:51.507
It's...it's the, um...


00:18:53.863 --> 00:18:55.946
...guys in red against the...
the guys in white.


00:18:56.103 --> 00:18:57.750
- White. I got it.
- Yeah. Yeah.


00:18:57.903 --> 00:18:59.911
Go, reds.


00:19:00.062 --> 00:19:01.743
Or White.


00:19:01.902 --> 00:19:03.582
You know.


00:19:47.299 --> 00:19:49.307
Oh, fuck.


00:19:52.299 --> 00:19:55.627
One bedroom, high ceilings.
Close to the PATH train.


00:19:55.779 --> 00:19:57.579
Ooh, washer dryer.


00:19:57.739 --> 00:20:00.303
- Plus it's crazy bright.
- Yeah.


00:20:00.458 --> 00:20:03.023
Well, that's morning light.


00:20:03.179 --> 00:20:05.023
I don't want that.


00:20:05.178 --> 00:20:08.027
Wow, that's, like,
your best excuse in two weeks.


00:20:08.178 --> 00:20:09.738
Hello, Koosers.


00:20:09.899 --> 00:20:11.818
- Did you sell that dresser?
- I did not.


00:20:11.978 --> 00:20:13.418
She's not interested
in the apartment, Henry.


00:20:13.578 --> 00:20:14.899
I told you.


00:20:15.058 --> 00:20:16.586
What?


00:20:16.738 --> 00:20:18.342
What do you mean,
"I told you"?


00:20:18.498 --> 00:20:21.182
You've been talking about
moving out for two years.


00:20:21.337 --> 00:20:23.105
You know what?
I'm saving money. Alright?


00:20:23.257 --> 00:20:25.265
I have a very definite plan.


00:20:25.417 --> 00:20:27.621
You mean that "stay at home,
corrode your soul" plan?


00:20:27.777 --> 00:20:29.741
No, no - the plan
where I move to the city


00:20:29.897 --> 00:20:31.381
and I work with
a big designer.


00:20:31.537 --> 00:20:33.665
I've already made
serious contacts.


00:20:33.817 --> 00:20:35.661
From where'?


00:20:35.817 --> 00:20:41.098
Huffman Koos? Well, you know me
and her and Marlon.


00:20:41.256 --> 00:20:43.941
Hey, I'm serious.
We're worried about you.


00:20:44.096 --> 00:20:46.256
OK, thank you.
I got it under control.


00:20:46.416 --> 00:20:47.943
You guys
go worry about yourselves.


00:20:50.896 --> 00:20:52.696
Wow. There she is'


00:20:52.855 --> 00:20:56.063
1 pm. Very impressive.


00:20:56.216 --> 00:20:58.496
So? Did you have fun
last night?


00:20:58.655 --> 00:21:00.335
I'm sure you'd love
a full report.


00:21:00.495 --> 00:21:02.504
You know,
some mothers and daughters


00:21:02.655 --> 00:21:05.295
actually talk about
these things, like friends.


00:21:05.454 --> 00:21:07.582
It's not happening.


00:21:07.735 --> 00:21:11.543
Well, maybe Toby will be
better company than you.


00:21:11.694 --> 00:21:13.102
Hi!


00:21:19.494 --> 00:21:21.218
Try and control yourself.


00:21:25.893 --> 00:21:27.137
Hey, Nina.


00:21:27.293 --> 00:21:30.337
- Morning, Cathy.
- Good morning, Tobias.


00:21:30.493 --> 00:21:33.134
- Uh, you forgot your sweater.
- Thank you.


00:21:33.293 --> 00:21:35.093
Can I get you
some breakfast, honey?


00:21:35.253 --> 00:21:37.457
No, thanks. I'm OK. Thanks.


00:21:38.932 --> 00:21:40.941
Well, I'll give you two
some privacy.


00:21:41.093 --> 00:21:43.820
There you are.


00:21:47.133 --> 00:21:48.933
I can hear you
hovering out there!


00:21:49.092 --> 00:21:50.620
Fine.


00:21:51.932 --> 00:21:53.613
You're looking a little crispy
this morning.


00:21:53.772 --> 00:21:55.813
Oh, thank you.
You can really put 'em away.


00:21:55.972 --> 00:21:58.733
Did I, uh...
Did I pass out?


00:21:58.892 --> 00:22:00.736
Yeah. Mmm, pretty much.


00:22:00.891 --> 00:22:03.095
Sorry about that.


00:22:03.251 --> 00:22:05.772
- No.
- Um...


00:22:06.931 --> 00:22:08.731
Look.
Uh, I was thinking.


00:22:08.891 --> 00:22:13.300
I had a really fun time last night
before passing out, and...


00:22:13.451 --> 00:22:15.579
...I'm supposed to have dinner
with my folks tonight.


00:22:15.731 --> 00:22:18.415
And being as
I'm leaving in two days,


00:22:18.570 --> 00:22:23.131
I thought, you know,
maybe you'd like to join us


00:22:23.290 --> 00:22:25.418
so we could
hang out more.


00:22:25.570 --> 00:22:30.534
Yeah. Dinner with you and
your parents, it...sounds great.


00:22:35.569 --> 00:22:37.773
- Come on, Toby.
- Hold.


00:22:39.609 --> 00:22:41.257
Alright. OK.


00:22:41.409 --> 00:22:43.329
- Let's go, Toby.
- Hold.


00:22:43.489 --> 00:22:47.178
Toby, it's called
the fast-moving tile game.


00:22:47.329 --> 00:22:49.249
Hold.


00:22:52.089 --> 00:22:53.976
- Let's go, Toby.
- Hold!


00:22:54.128 --> 00:22:56.496
OK. OK.


00:22:56.649 --> 00:22:58.296
Actually,
just go out ahead of me.


00:22:58.448 --> 00:23:00.172
Oh!


00:23:00.328 --> 00:23:02.848
5, the 13. I'm out!


00:23:03.008 --> 00:23:05.615
- What?
- Ah. Yes.


00:23:05.768 --> 00:23:07.328
Now, who's gonna help me
with the dishes?


00:23:07.488 --> 00:23:08.971
I will, Mom. Wait.


00:23:09.128 --> 00:23:11.048
Hang on a sec.
I gotta take this. It's work.


00:23:11.207 --> 00:23:12.767
This is Toby.


00:23:12.927 --> 00:23:14.411
Oh, hello, sir.


00:23:14.567 --> 00:23:15.888
Uh-huh.


00:23:16.047 --> 00:23:17.367
- No, no, it's no problem.
- Yeah.


00:23:17.527 --> 00:23:19.207
I think maybe
I'll go pick up a movie


00:23:19.367 --> 00:23:20.850
in case you want to
watch something later.


00:23:21.007 --> 00:23:23.811
- That sounds fun.
- I'll come with you.


00:23:23.966 --> 00:23:26.574
Keep you company
while Toby does the dishes.


00:23:37.166 --> 00:23:38.529
Look.


00:23:38.686 --> 00:23:41.729
What happened last night
was a mistake.


00:23:41.886 --> 00:23:44.134
- OK?
- No, you're right.


00:23:46.885 --> 00:23:50.050
Relax, OK?
It was nothing.


00:23:50.205 --> 00:23:52.409
And you stopped it.
You're absolved.


00:24:02.724 --> 00:24:04.372
Hello in there?


00:24:04.524 --> 00:24:06.085
Is there anyone in there?


00:24:06.244 --> 00:24:09.168
You just have to
instigate trouble.


00:24:09.324 --> 00:24:12.128
I do not instigate trouble.


00:24:12.284 --> 00:24:13.604
Well, OK.


00:24:13.763 --> 00:24:15.291
Well, then, Why'd you
come to dinner tonight?


00:24:15.443 --> 00:24:16.764
Toby invited me.


00:24:16.923 --> 00:24:18.691
And now that we're
talking about instigators,


00:24:18.843 --> 00:24:20.687
you leaned into me.


00:24:20.843 --> 00:24:22.404
I leaned into you?


00:24:22.563 --> 00:24:24.407
- I leaned... I did not lean.
- Yes, you did.


00:24:24.563 --> 00:24:26.124
- You leaned into me.
- What?!


00:24:26.283 --> 00:24:28.291
Oh... He said, she said.


00:24:29.962 --> 00:24:31.283
He said, she said.


00:24:31.442 --> 00:24:33.122
Where did that come from?


00:24:33.282 --> 00:24:35.202
I have no idea
where that came from.


00:24:41.402 --> 00:24:43.246
I'm not instigating.


00:25:08.680 --> 00:25:10.044
I've been thinking
about getting


00:25:10.200 --> 00:25:12.209
one of those
giant electric snow globes.


00:25:12.360 --> 00:25:15.404
You ever seen one of those?
Really big ones?


00:25:15.560 --> 00:25:17.568
Fantastic.


00:25:17.720 --> 00:25:19.684
Mom?


00:25:19.839 --> 00:25:21.923
We're in here, honey.


00:25:22.079 --> 00:25:24.567
I'm going out.


00:25:24.719 --> 00:25:26.803
Well!


00:25:26.960 --> 00:25:29.480
Well, don't you look nice?


00:25:29.639 --> 00:25:31.167
Thanks.


00:25:31.319 --> 00:25:32.760
So is Toby
taking you somewhere?


00:25:32.919 --> 00:25:35.680
- Uh, yeah.
- OK. OK.


00:25:35.839 --> 00:25:37.203
- Fine.
- Mom!


00:25:37.359 --> 00:25:39.083
Give me some room.


00:25:39.238 --> 00:25:41.519
Fine. Have fun.


00:25:45.438 --> 00:25:47.043
Is she eating with us?


00:25:47.198 --> 00:25:50.079
Toby is taking her out.
She was all dressed up.


00:25:50.238 --> 00:25:51.962
- Toby already left for DC.
- What?


00:25:52.118 --> 00:25:53.525
Yeah, first thing
this morning.


00:25:53.678 --> 00:25:55.522
Some congressman wanted
to be with the delegation


00:25:55.677 --> 00:25:57.238
before they went to China.


00:26:26.716 --> 00:26:29.716
"Left this morning."
Oh, shit!


00:26:41.874 --> 00:26:43.958
- H-hello?
- Mom?


00:26:44.115 --> 00:26:46.123
Listen. I lied earlier.


00:26:46.274 --> 00:26:48.042
I'm not going out with Toby.


00:26:48.194 --> 00:26:49.918
He actually left for Washington
this morning.


00:26:50.074 --> 00:26:52.801
- Oh?
- Yeah.


00:26:52.954 --> 00:26:57.121
I'm meeting Meredith Lovett.
Remember her?


00:26:57.274 --> 00:26:59.597
I didn't tell you because
I know you don't like her.


00:26:59.754 --> 00:27:03.802
Oh, honey, thank you.
Thank you for telling me.


00:27:03.953 --> 00:27:07.761
You know...
You don't have to lie to me.


00:27:07.913 --> 00:27:09.954
I know.


00:27:10.113 --> 00:27:11.837
So where are you going?


00:27:13.433 --> 00:27:16.641
Uh, we're going to the Regal
to see a movie.


00:27:18.632 --> 00:27:19.953
Uh, Mom?


00:27:20.112 --> 00:27:22.632
Thanks...for being so cool


00:27:22.792 --> 00:27:25.040
and letting me come back
and stay and everything.


00:27:25.192 --> 00:27:28.040
I've been feeling really
tossed around lately, so...


00:27:28.191 --> 00:27:31.596
You know.
Thanks for being there.


00:27:33.072 --> 00:27:35.472
OK, well...
I'll see you later for dinner.


00:27:40.431 --> 00:27:41.991
Oh, my...


00:28:18.829 --> 00:28:20.073
Whoa!


00:28:20.229 --> 00:28:22.270
Cathy.


00:28:22.429 --> 00:28:24.632
- What are you...?
- I'm, uh...


00:28:24.789 --> 00:28:27.233
- What are you...
- I'm not, uh... Nothing.


00:28:27.389 --> 00:28:30.913
Paige and I had a fight,
and I spent the night here. So...


00:28:32.828 --> 00:28:35.272
Oh, my God!


00:28:35.428 --> 00:28:37.032
Hey, Nina.


00:28:37.187 --> 00:28:38.628
- What are you...
- Oh, my God!


00:28:38.788 --> 00:28:40.228
Cathy! Slow down.


00:28:40.388 --> 00:28:43.595
Slow down? I can read
an ice bucket, David.


00:28:43.748 --> 00:28:45.789
- Cathy.
- Oh, my God!


00:28:45.947 --> 00:28:48.795
I'm gonna throw up!


00:28:53.906 --> 00:28:56.427
- Jesus, David!
- Paige, listen to me.


00:28:56.587 --> 00:28:58.507
Just tell me how long
it's been going on.


00:28:58.667 --> 00:29:00.827
We kissed. That's it.


00:29:00.987 --> 00:29:03.431
Then what the hell were you
doing in a goddamn motel room?


00:29:03.586 --> 00:29:05.234
This...


00:29:06.986 --> 00:29:09.506
I'm sorry.
The whole thing was wrong.


00:29:09.666 --> 00:29:10.987
But let's be honest.


00:29:11.146 --> 00:29:13.230
Things have not been good
between us for a long time.


00:29:13.385 --> 00:29:14.869
Oh, God, don't do that.


00:29:15.025 --> 00:29:17.425
Don't apologise and then
blame me in the same sentence.


00:29:17.586 --> 00:29:19.594
Come on, Paige.
You're not happy either.


00:29:19.745 --> 00:29:22.146
It's not about
being happy, David!


00:29:22.305 --> 00:29:24.225
Well, then, what is it?


00:29:43.784 --> 00:29:45.552
Jesus, say something already.


00:29:45.704 --> 00:29:47.668
I will say something
when I want.


00:29:47.823 --> 00:29:50.224
You don't get to decide
when I say something. I decide!


00:29:50.384 --> 00:29:52.828
- Then decide already!
- I'll decide.


00:29:52.984 --> 00:29:56.268
You have caused
some serious trouble


00:29:56.424 --> 00:29:57.711
in the past, young lady.


00:29:57.863 --> 00:29:59.271
Don't you
roll your eyes at me.


00:29:59.423 --> 00:30:01.387
I'm sorry, it doesn't work
when you try to play


00:30:01.543 --> 00:30:03.267
the stern father - it looks like
you're pretending.


00:30:03.423 --> 00:30:05.507
Your father is not pretending!
We are furious!


00:30:05.662 --> 00:30:07.070
I'm not pretending.


00:30:07.223 --> 00:30:08.783
David and I,
we like each other.


00:30:08.942 --> 00:30:11.190
- Oh, my God.
- We've always been close.


00:30:11.342 --> 00:30:13.383
It's not like we planned this.
It just happened.


00:30:13.542 --> 00:30:15.147
- You like each other?
- Yeah.


00:30:15.302 --> 00:30:16.623
- Oh, my God.
- Oh, my God!


00:30:16.782 --> 00:30:19.302
I know what this is -
this is some sick revenge


00:30:19.462 --> 00:30:21.349
