00:45:09.129 --> 00:45:11.409
he went online and found
a pick-up ultimate frisbee game


00:45:11.568 --> 00:45:12.932
in Paramus.


00:45:13.088 --> 00:45:16.132
Hey, guys! You, uh...
you got room for one more?


00:45:16.288 --> 00:45:18.372
No daylight. No daylight.


00:45:18.528 --> 00:45:23.328
So it was really Jared Kass
and I, and Joel Silver...


00:45:23.488 --> 00:45:25.168
Joel Silver,
the movie producer?


00:45:25.328 --> 00:45:26.572
Yeah. Yeah.


00:45:27.648 --> 00:45:29.131
My mother
had been making herself


00:45:29.287 --> 00:45:30.968
mysteriously unavailable.


00:45:32.127 --> 00:45:34.331
But, as all our neighbours
discovered...


00:45:35.927 --> 00:45:39.092
...she hadn't completely lost sight
of the Christmas spirit.


00:45:44.287 --> 00:45:45.695
Terry!


00:45:45.846 --> 00:45:47.526
Everything was changing.


00:45:47.687 --> 00:45:49.007
Terry!


00:45:49.166 --> 00:45:50.771
No-one even recognised
each other anymore.


00:45:53.606 --> 00:45:56.367
- Smoothie?
- Oh, good God.


00:45:59.446 --> 00:46:01.486
Very good.


00:46:01.646 --> 00:46:03.729
Now kiss the chef.


00:46:15.525 --> 00:46:17.533
Maybe they are
really in love.


00:46:17.685 --> 00:46:19.005
You said it doesn't last.


00:46:19.164 --> 00:46:21.445
You said that the grasses only
wanted the cows for their money.


00:46:21.605 --> 00:46:23.165
Usually that is the case,
but not always.


00:46:23.324 --> 00:46:25.332
- Your dad is pretty cute.
- Don't be gross, OK?


00:46:25.484 --> 00:46:27.328
Just because you haven't gotten
laid in, like, three weeks.


00:46:27.484 --> 00:46:29.448
Perhaps your problem is
more with Nina than your father.


00:46:29.604 --> 00:46:31.371
Oh, is that so, Henry?
Why is that?


00:46:31.524 --> 00:46:32.844
Because maybe
you are jealous,


00:46:33.003 --> 00:46:36.244
because she has travelled
many places and has lived,


00:46:36.404 --> 00:46:39.165
because she takes chances.


00:46:39.323 --> 00:46:40.644
No. You know what?


00:46:40.804 --> 00:46:42.331
You, my friend,
have breathed in


00:46:42.483 --> 00:46:44.327
a little too much
of this cheap pine wax, OK?


00:46:44.483 --> 00:46:47.364
'Cause she's a selfish skank.
And he's selfish too.


00:46:47.523 --> 00:46:49.804
Yeah, but if he
really is happier with her


00:46:49.963 --> 00:46:51.327
and you make him stop,


00:46:51.483 --> 00:46:53.043
then you're the one
who's being selfish.


00:46:54.883 --> 00:46:56.563
That is maybe
the most intelligent thing


00:46:56.722 --> 00:46:58.162
you have ever said.


00:47:13.801 --> 00:47:15.569
Hey.


00:47:15.721 --> 00:47:18.569
What is
Barnyard International?


00:47:18.721 --> 00:47:21.722
Well, um... See those presents
you got at babyGap?


00:47:21.881 --> 00:47:24.009
Instead of giving those
to a baby


00:47:24.160 --> 00:47:25.721
who might already
have lots of clothes,


00:47:25.881 --> 00:47:27.801
why not help a baby
who doesn't have any food?


00:47:27.961 --> 00:47:29.281
They're not for a baby.


00:47:29.440 --> 00:47:30.881
They're for my husband's
new girlfriend.


00:47:33.000 --> 00:47:34.484
Here's some pamphlets.


00:47:36.920 --> 00:47:39.364
"One goat
can provide a family


00:47:39.519 --> 00:47:41.647
"with enough milk
for an entire year."


00:47:43.440 --> 00:47:45.568
It's like the Christmas gift
that keeps giving.


00:47:45.719 --> 00:47:47.279
Yeah. It is.


00:47:47.440 --> 00:47:49.360
That's good. Can I use that?


00:47:49.519 --> 00:47:51.963
Sure.


00:47:59.319 --> 00:48:01.566
Oh, yes! Oh! Oh!


00:48:09.278 --> 00:48:12.278
There are gift receipts inside,
if anyone wants to return them.


00:48:15.918 --> 00:48:17.642
I think after Christmas Eve,


00:48:17.797 --> 00:48:20.242
we should demand
that Paige have dinner with us.


00:48:23.197 --> 00:48:24.877
What are you doing?


00:48:25.037 --> 00:48:26.684
Come here.


00:48:28.837 --> 00:48:31.237
- I have toothpaste in my mouth.
- I don't care.


00:48:36.436 --> 00:48:38.160
Come here.


00:48:48.836 --> 00:48:51.880
OK. Thank you
for dropping me off.


00:48:52.036 --> 00:48:54.077
I got you these.


00:48:59.155 --> 00:49:00.955
Chef's clogs.


00:49:01.115 --> 00:49:03.002
You said after working last night,
your feet hurt, so...


00:49:03.154 --> 00:49:04.834
You're so sweet.


00:49:13.474 --> 00:49:15.318
OK. You're gonna
make me late.


00:49:15.474 --> 00:49:17.274
Whoo!


00:49:27.033 --> 00:49:28.353
- That was fast.
- Yeah.


00:49:28.514 --> 00:49:30.674
Um...


00:49:30.833 --> 00:49:32.317
What?


00:49:34.473 --> 00:49:35.793
Nothing.


00:49:35.952 --> 00:49:37.273
What's up?


00:49:37.433 --> 00:49:38.754
Nothing.


00:49:38.913 --> 00:49:40.517
Come on.
Tell me what's wrong.


00:49:42.432 --> 00:49:44.713
- I...
- I love you, Nina.


00:49:46.672 --> 00:49:50.153
You shit. You suck.
I wanted to say it first.


00:49:51.912 --> 00:49:54.673
Well, now I'm not saying it.
You blew it, buddy.


00:49:56.671 --> 00:49:58.875
I'm just kidding.
I love you too.


00:50:03.791 --> 00:50:06.431
You guys were married
for 28 years.


00:50:06.591 --> 00:50:08.839
If anyone should call,
it should be him.


00:50:08.990 --> 00:50:11.031
- Do you have any perfume?
- No.


00:50:11.190 --> 00:50:13.875
What?! Where are you
even going?


00:50:14.031 --> 00:50:16.431
Well, I read about
a late-evening cabaret show


00:50:16.590 --> 00:50:18.074
that begins at 9:30.


00:50:18.230 --> 00:50:20.478
- I'm taking myself out.
- Cabaret?


00:50:20.631 --> 00:50:22.759
Am I the only one
who's dealing with this?


00:50:22.910 --> 00:50:26.511
I mean, don't you
want to come back home?


00:50:28.469 --> 00:50:29.910
I'm not sure.


00:50:30.070 --> 00:50:32.590
I'm having a good time
for once.


00:50:32.749 --> 00:50:36.677
I'd like to see you
do the same.


00:50:40.269 --> 00:50:41.796
Let's go, guys!
Pick up the pace!


00:50:41.949 --> 00:50:43.629
Hey, Mondo!
Where's my rigatoni? Let's go!


00:50:43.789 --> 00:50:45.273
Bring it up, parmigiana.


00:50:45.429 --> 00:50:47.229
Nina! Plate 27!


00:50:47.388 --> 00:50:48.752
Alright, guys-


00:50:48.908 --> 00:50:51.232
On 24, I got a mahi mahi
and a chicken parmigiana.


00:50:51.388 --> 00:50:53.275
Thanks for sending her to me.
She's a good worker.


00:50:53.428 --> 00:50:54.836
- Well, that's great.
- Chef likes her.


00:50:54.988 --> 00:50:58.153
Haven't seen you and Paige
for a while. It's good to see you.


00:50:58.308 --> 00:51:00.753
- Enjoy.
- Thanks.


00:51:29.666 --> 00:51:32.590
- Done with your appetiser, sir?
- Sorry?


00:51:32.746 --> 00:51:34.274
Done with
your appetiser, sir?


00:51:34.425 --> 00:51:36.389
Yeah. That... Yeah.
That's great. Thanks.


00:51:41.106 --> 00:51:42.633
Hello.


00:51:43.945 --> 00:51:45.473
Hi, Paige.


00:51:47.465 --> 00:51:49.952
Nice move
on the Christmas card.


00:51:50.105 --> 00:51:51.752
Thank you.


00:51:52.785 --> 00:51:55.906
- Dining alone?
- Uh, yeah. I guess.


00:51:57.224 --> 00:51:59.068
So how are you doing?
Is everything...


00:51:59.225 --> 00:52:01.025
Sit down. Don't have to
make this uncomfortable.


00:52:01.184 --> 00:52:02.667
Just...


00:52:05.304 --> 00:52:07.552
Plus, you know
how I hate pleasantries.


00:52:09.064 --> 00:52:11.148
What about you?


00:52:11.303 --> 00:52:13.311
You look happy.


00:52:14.704 --> 00:52:16.264
Things are OK.
You know, I'm...


00:52:16.423 --> 00:52:18.868
If you're happy,
you can say so.


00:52:19.023 --> 00:52:20.790
You don't need
to spare my feelings.


00:52:20.943 --> 00:52:24.827
Just...be genuine,
David, please.


00:52:24.983 --> 00:52:26.587
Please.


00:52:28.983 --> 00:52:31.143
Yes. I'm happy-


00:52:34.542 --> 00:52:36.102
Thank you.


00:52:36.262 --> 00:52:37.822
Yeah.


00:52:39.222 --> 00:52:41.142
Look, I know
there's nothing I can say...


00:52:41.302 --> 00:52:42.710
Then don't try.


00:52:42.861 --> 00:52:44.661
Paige, stop. Please.


00:52:44.821 --> 00:52:47.069
This is exactly
how we got to this.


00:52:48.462 --> 00:52:52.903
OK, not exactly.
It's partly.


00:52:53.061 --> 00:52:55.909
We stopped talking
to each other.


00:52:58.261 --> 00:53:00.825
I used to love who I was
around you.


00:53:00.980 --> 00:53:03.708
What happened to us?


00:53:05.260 --> 00:53:07.748
We used to have fun.
Remember that?


00:53:09.700 --> 00:53:12.221
We used to laugh.
God, you were so funny.


00:53:12.380 --> 00:53:14.027
I'm still funny.


00:53:14.180 --> 00:53:16.264
I'm... Ask them.


00:53:38.219 --> 00:53:39.986
Shelly just fired me!


00:53:40.139 --> 00:53:41.666
Hey, hey.


00:53:41.818 --> 00:53:45.145
- What happened?
- Oh! This is fucking bullshit!


00:53:45.298 --> 00:53:47.862
- What? Why?
- Because he's not an idiot.


00:53:48.018 --> 00:53:50.778
He saw you and Paige, and he
saw me, and he figured it out.


00:53:50.938 --> 00:53:53.261
He said he didn't want
to be in the middle of it.


00:53:53.418 --> 00:53:55.426
And I was good at that job!


00:53:55.577 --> 00:53:57.541
Why...


00:53:57.698 --> 00:53:59.978
Why were you talking to her?


00:54:00.137 --> 00:54:01.817
She came into the restaurant.


00:54:01.976 --> 00:54:04.737
What do you expect me to do?


00:54:04.897 --> 00:54:07.220
I saw you sitting with her,
and I just thought...


00:54:09.777 --> 00:54:11.097
Thought what?


00:54:11.257 --> 00:54:13.024
I don't know.


00:54:15.496 --> 00:54:17.384
You looked normal together.


00:54:24.615 --> 00:54:27.223
Can we please get out of here?


00:54:35.294 --> 00:54:36.658
# I really can't stay


00:54:36.814 --> 00:54:38.614
# But, baby,
it's cold outside


00:54:38.775 --> 00:54:41.655
- # I've got to go away
- # But, baby, it's cold outside


00:54:41.815 --> 00:54:43.419
# This evening has been...


00:54:43.574 --> 00:54:45.102
# Been hoping
that you drop in


00:54:45.254 --> 00:54:46.618
# So very nice


00:54:46.774 --> 00:54:49.818
# I'll hold your hands
They're just like ice


00:54:49.974 --> 00:54:51.774
# My mother
will start to worry... I


00:54:51.934 --> 00:54:53.701
Hi. Mrs Ostroff'?


00:54:53.854 --> 00:54:55.501
We've never met.


00:54:55.654 --> 00:54:57.782
But I'm Ethan.


00:55:02.574 --> 00:55:04.298
You're our leader.
You can't quit!


00:55:04.453 --> 00:55:07.694
Christmas Eve is in, like,
six days. They're counting on us.


00:55:07.853 --> 00:55:12.021
Try and calm down. Calm down.


00:55:12.173 --> 00:55:15.054
Calm down. Order!


00:55:15.212 --> 00:55:17.099
I know you're upset.


00:55:17.253 --> 00:55:20.821
But you're all
dedicated and talented singers.


00:55:22.292 --> 00:55:23.613
Marcus will take over
as leader.


00:55:23.772 --> 00:55:26.096
- What?!
- Marcus?


00:55:26.252 --> 00:55:28.216
- Why are you even doing this?
- Yeah.


00:55:28.371 --> 00:55:32.015
Well, I believe these pamphlets
should explain everything.


00:55:32.172 --> 00:55:34.856
Each cow or goat
will allow its recipient


00:55:35.011 --> 00:55:37.619
independence
and self-sufficiency


00:55:37.771 --> 00:55:40.052
for years to come.


00:55:41.051 --> 00:55:43.255
And that's pretty great,
isn't it?


00:55:44.571 --> 00:55:47.419
Shelly, this has
nothing to do with you.


00:55:47.570 --> 00:55:49.414
No, I know it's complicated.


00:55:49.571 --> 00:55:51.655
No. I understand.


00:55:53.090 --> 00:55:54.858
Thanks for calling back.


00:55:57.690 --> 00:55:59.011
Told you.


00:55:59.170 --> 00:56:00.894
He'll write you
a reference, but...


00:56:01.050 --> 00:56:02.654
Yeah. He doesn't
want to get involved.


00:56:02.809 --> 00:56:06.291
This isn't gonna work.
I need to find another job.


00:56:06.450 --> 00:56:08.130
I can't stay at Meredith's
rent-free.


00:56:08.289 --> 00:56:09.610
I know.


00:56:09.770 --> 00:56:11.090
And I can't stay here,


00:56:11.249 --> 00:56:12.657
across the street
from my parents.


00:56:12.809 --> 00:56:15.570
- I love you. But...
- What the fuck?


00:56:15.729 --> 00:56:19.133
- Ethan?
- What the hell is going on?


00:56:19.289 --> 00:56:22.377
- What are you doing here?
- Ethan? Like, Ethan Ethan?


00:56:22.529 --> 00:56:25.410
- How did you get in here?
- Your mom gave me the keys.


00:56:25.568 --> 00:56:27.216
She told me
to let myself in,


00:56:27.368 --> 00:56:28.896
like you might not
hear the bell.


00:56:29.048 --> 00:56:31.568
Look, Ethan, I'm sorry, but I'm
gonna have to ask you to leave.


00:56:31.728 --> 00:56:35.132
You can ask, but I'm not gonna.
Who is this?


00:56:35.287 --> 00:56:37.175
Ethan, this is David -
David and Paige,


00:56:37.328 --> 00:56:39.292
my parents' best friends
from across the street.


00:56:40.527 --> 00:56:42.087
Why are you telling
your parents' friend


00:56:42.248 --> 00:56:43.568
that you love him?


00:56:43.727 --> 00:56:45.975
The door's open.
What's going on?


00:56:46.127 --> 00:56:48.375
Nina, I need to talk to you.


00:56:48.527 --> 00:56:50.611
Can we go somewhere
for, like, five minutes?


00:56:50.767 --> 00:56:52.447
Ethan!
I think you should leave.


00:56:52.607 --> 00:56:55.455
- Ethan Ethan?
- Yes! Just five minutes!


00:56:55.606 --> 00:56:57.526
She said no, Ethan.


00:56:57.686 --> 00:56:59.934
I'm gonna ask you one more time
to get out of here.


00:57:00.087 --> 00:57:04.735
And if I don't, Pops,
what are you gonna do about it?


00:57:04.886 --> 00:57:05.846
Arggh!


00:57:06.005 --> 00:57:07.413
'Dad!
Hey!


00:57:07.566 --> 00:57:08.406
- David!
- Dad!


00:57:08.566 --> 00:57:10.170
Get off me!


00:57:11.606 --> 00:57:13.854
# Your eyes
are like starlight now


00:57:14.005 --> 00:57:15.533
# To break this spell


00:57:15.685 --> 00:57:18.566
# I'll take your hat
Your hair looks swell... #


00:57:18.725 --> 00:57:20.525
Why don't you go fuck...


00:57:20.685 --> 00:57:23.412
- What?
- Nothing.


00:57:23.564 --> 00:57:25.169
Its OK.


00:57:27.844 --> 00:57:32.045
# Baby,
it's cold outside. #


00:57:41.964 --> 00:57:45.892
Yes, I cheated on you.
And for that, I am deeply sorry.


00:57:46.044 --> 00:57:49.132
But here's the thing.
I'm a sabotager.


00:57:49.283 --> 00:57:52.884
See, any time
anything good happens to me,


00:57:53.043 --> 00:57:54.887
I...I...I just try
and ruin it, you know,


00:57:55.043 --> 00:57:56.603
because I get scared.


00:57:56.763 --> 00:58:00.451
Now, things with us
were really...real.


00:58:00.602 --> 00:58:03.210
But I didn't feel like
I deserved you,


00:58:03.362 --> 00:58:06.963
so I became the sabotager
and, like, destroyed it.


00:58:07.122 --> 00:58:09.086
That's great, Ethan.


00:58:09.242 --> 00:58:11.326
But we can't just go on
and pretend like everything's fine


00:58:11.482 --> 00:58:13.010
because you learned
a new term about yourself.


00:58:13.162 --> 00:58:16.731
And I don't even think
'sabotager' is a word.


00:58:16.882 --> 00:58:18.769
OK. Please allow me
to finish.


00:58:18.922 --> 00:58:21.966
See, I think
you're a sabotager also.


00:58:22.121 --> 00:58:25.165
You totally pushed for us
to get married so you could, like,


00:58:25.321 --> 00:58:27.525
prove to your parents
that, you know,


00:58:27.681 --> 00:58:29.089
you were
this responsible person.


00:58:29.241 --> 00:58:33.082
But simultaneously, you were
just trying to piss them off


00:58:33.240 --> 00:58:35.160
by marrying someone like me.


00:58:35.320 --> 00:58:36.848
I've moved on.


00:58:37.001 --> 00:58:39.324
- OK? David and I...
- David and you...


00:58:39.481 --> 00:58:43.845
He's your parents' best friend.
For Christ's sakes.


00:58:44.000 --> 00:58:47.121
I mean, what... Are you gonna move
here to New Jersey?


00:58:47.280 --> 00:58:49.528
You hate it here.


00:58:51.639 --> 00:58:52.960
We're done.


00:58:53.119 --> 00:58:55.247
OK? Go home.


00:58:55.400 --> 00:58:56.927
I only bought
a one-way ticket.


00:58:59.960 --> 00:59:01.968
Well, I'm not giving up
on us, Nina!


00:59:02.119 --> 00:59:04.400
I love you too much
for that!


00:59:07.159 --> 00:59:09.319
What?


00:59:35.797 --> 00:59:37.357
What are you doing
with my bag?


00:59:37.517 --> 00:59:39.525
Huh? Nothing.
Just getting it some air.


00:59:41.757 --> 00:59:43.918
- Give me my bag.
- No.


00:59:44.077 --> 00:59:46.280
Give me my bag!


00:59:46.437 --> 00:59:49.601
- Eat me, dick slut.
- Give me my bag, Vanessa!


00:59:49.756 --> 00:59:51.239
No, Nina!


00:59:51.396 --> 00:59:53.316
- No!
- Give me my bag!


00:59:53.476 --> 00:59:56.836
- No! No!
- Give it to me!


00:59:56.996 --> 00:59:58.317
- Whoa, whoa, whoa!
- Give it!


00:59:58.476 --> 00:59:59.959
Oh!


01:00:35.033 --> 01:00:36.877
Oh, honey. Uh...


01:00:37.034 --> 01:00:38.714
Honey?


01:00:38.873 --> 01:00:40.793
I'm sorry, Dad.


01:00:40.953 --> 01:00:42.753
Uh...


01:00:48.312 --> 01:00:50.473
Oh...


01:01:03.472 --> 01:01:06.276
Uh, you know, leave it be.
It's a...it's a badge of honour.


01:01:06.431 --> 01:01:07.872
- You sure?
- Yeah.


01:01:08.032 --> 01:01:09.876
There's aloe on the pad
to prevent scarring.


01:01:10.031 --> 01:01:11.515
OK. Um...


01:01:11.671 --> 01:01:17.040
You know, I'm good.
I'm, uh...I'm good.


01:01:19.030 --> 01:01:21.398
I'm so sorry about
all this horrible...


01:01:22.791 --> 01:01:24.318
...stuff.


01:01:25.591 --> 01:01:27.119
I'm just...


01:01:28.471 --> 01:01:30.315
Yeah.


01:01:33.590 --> 01:01:37.278
You know,
my parents were kinda weird.


01:01:37.430 --> 01:01:40.234
That's why I'm, um...


01:01:41.590 --> 01:01:46.194
Sometimes it's really hard
to say everything you want to.


01:01:46.349 --> 01:01:47.909
You know...


01:01:49.389 --> 01:01:53.797
Your father, he loves you.


01:01:54.989 --> 01:01:57.989
Just don't let that
get confused


01:01:58.148 --> 01:02:00.396
with everything
that's happening.


01:02:04.548 --> 01:02:05.911
Life.


01:02:06.068 --> 01:02:07.388
Ooph!


01:02:07.548 --> 01:02:09.076
